# Gas-unstable continuation (S:1088): the forming satellite (Regime 0) is the wind host (D:103); the
# wind ejects its cold gas and then, by the HOST's Regime 0, its CGM pair (M:397-417); the cold gas
# gone, the yield takes its all-metals branch (S:1104-1108) to the FoF central's hot metals by the
# central's Regime 1. The instability burst forms no stars.
# The real rows of cgm_sf_r4_snap32_hot_group
# (/Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R4/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256
# 2b606ee7ac82559e32c7c91161f1edb44f89288ec57016e80da884e118ed0807)), the satellite's ColdGas and
# MetalsColdGas raised x5 so its disk is gas-unstable after feedback (as c05's unstable r0_ fixtures
# raise theirs).
# galaxy 0: R4 Snap_32 row 70 (GalaxyIndex 182, Type 0, Regime 1)
# galaxy 1: R4 Snap_32 row 71 (GalaxyIndex 197, Type 1, Regime 0)
